      <title>Chris Rokos: No, Tax Isn't Driving UK Billionaires to Athens</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-09-16/chris-rokos-no-tax-isn-t-driving-uk-billionaires-to-athens</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">946faa43b2ba6666007e3bce</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 04:00:07 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>There are two certainties in life: death, and taxes getting the blame whenever rich people leave the UK. Billionaire hedge fund manager Chris Rokos departing for Greece, where he’ll pay just €100,000 ($115,000) a year, is the latest to provoke a flood of recriminations. But these stories — and claims of an exodus of the super-rich from Britain — should be taken with a hefty dose of salt.</description>
